From a42710aa63bddd85ed52fd55d040bccbc0a38b9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 18:52:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: uio: Add binding for uio-fwu-shmem
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The "uio-fwu-shmem" compatible is used on STM32MP2x boards in the M33TD
configuration to expose a memory-mapped region to userspace through the
generic UIO platform driver (uio_pdrv_genirq). This region holds the
Firmware Update (FWU) images used by the Cortex-M33 coprocessor.

The node is bound to uio_pdrv_genirq via the
"uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id=uio-fwu-shmem" kernel command line parameter.

Until now this compatible was only present in the device trees, with no
schema describing it, causing "dtbs_check" to report:

  uio-fwu-shmem@81300000: failed to match any schema with compatible:
  ['uio-fwu-shmem']

Add the missing binding to document the compatible and fix the warning.

Change-Id: Ia37c25fec14739368bf594dbf3172701f5437131
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-4.8
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/579101
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 .../bindings/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml           | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..755db0033198
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/uio/uio-fwu-shmem.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Userspace I/O (UIO) shared memory for Firmware Update (FWU)
+
+maintainers:
+  - Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
+
+description:
+  A memory-mapped region exported to userspace through the Linux UIO
+  framework. It holds the Firmware Update (FWU) images that are used by
+  the coprocessor's update agent. The node is bound to the generic UIO
+  platform driver (uio_pdrv_genirq) through the
+  "uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id=uio-fwu-shmem" kernel command line parameter.
+
+properties:
+  $nodename:
+    pattern: "^uio-fwu-shmem(@[0-9a-f]+)?$"
+
+  compatible:
+    const: uio-fwu-shmem
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    soc {
+        #address-cells = <2>;
+        #size-cells = <2>;
+
+        uio-fwu-shmem@81300000 {
+            compatible = "uio-fwu-shmem";
+            reg = <0x0 0x81300000 0x0 0x00a00000>;
+        };
+    };
-- 
